  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Clinic Appointment Book",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Clinic Appointment Book\"**\n\nThe three signed-in panels (requester, interpreter and Academy team) work like a calm clinic agenda. A list of things that happen at a time starts with the day and the time in a fixed left column, so you scan it the way a receptionist scans the day's book. Each screen answers two questions: what is waiting on me, and what comes next. Nothing decorative sits between the person and their next action. The system rejects the card-grid dashboard that leads with stats tiles.\n\nThe material is light and clinical. Content sits on a cool, faintly blue-tinted near-white ground, on white sheets with hairline borders. The text is ink-navy. Brand blue appears in only two places, the active location and the primary action. State colours (green for confirmed, amber for waiting, red for refused or disputed) appear as small dots and quiet pills, and they are dark enough to read as text. Public Sans, an institutional workhorse, sets every word, with tabular figures wherever numbers line up. Red Hat Mono is kept for request codes, references, IBANs and audit actions. Density is moderate: 36px controls, 14px agenda rows and 12px table cells.\n\n**Scope.** This world applies to the three panels (`<html class=\"app-panel\">` in `admin-web`, `requester-web` and `interpreter-web`), where shared components opt into it through the `panel:` variant. It also applies to the public site's inner pages through the page banner (cool ground, ink title, short brand-blue rule) and the solid ink-navy closing band. The site home is **out of scope**. It keeps its older look (gradient hero, Plus Jakarta Sans, lifted cards) by the Academy's decision, and nothing here governs it. The site does not set `app-panel`, so its inner pages still render in Plus Jakarta Sans with the root tokens (12px radius, the older shadow scale).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Time comes first: a 76px tabular column with the day above the time leads every timed list.",
      "Cool ground, white sheets, 1px hairlines. Depth comes from tone, not from lift.",
      "Brand blue only marks the active place and the primary action.",
      "State is carried by a dot and a word together, never by fill alone.",
      "Public Sans everywhere with tabular numbers. Red Hat Mono for codes.",
      "Portuguese for everything the user reads."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Places Rule",
        "body": "Brand blue marks where you are (the active navigation item, today in the agenda) and what you do next (the primary button). It is never decorative fill. One primary action per page header.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dot-and-Word Rule",
        "body": "Every status shows its colour as a 6px dot in `currentColor` beside a Portuguese label. Colour never carries state alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every table, and every element marked `tabular-nums`, sets numbers in tabular figures, so times, kwanza amounts and counts line up in columns.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is For Machines Rule",
        "body": "Red Hat Mono is used only for identifiers a person might copy or quote back. It is never used for labels, headings or emphasis.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper, Not Plastic Rule",
        "body": "In the panels, nothing at rest lifts, glows or translates on hover. Hover changes a background tone (quiet fill, or blue wash at 40–50%) over 150ms, and that is all.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** lead every list of timed things with the agenda column (day above time, 76px, tabular), and keep it as the first column of timed tables.",
      "**Do** keep brand blue to the active place and the primary action (the Two Places Rule). Use one primary button per page header.",
      "**Do** show state as a dot plus a Portuguese word on a 10% tint of the state colour.",
      "**Do** use tabular figures for times, kwanza amounts and counts, and Red Hat Mono for codes and references.",
      "**Do** keep sheets flat: white, 1px hairline, 10px corners, sheet shadow only. Hover is a tone change over 150ms.",
      "**Do** put \"what waits on me\" before \"everything\" on overviews, and first on phones.",
      "**Do** give every list its empty, loading and error states in plain Portuguese."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** open a panel with a grid of stats tiles. The agenda and the waiting list are the first view.",
      "**Don't** use gradients, glows, lifted or translating hover, or `scale` press effects inside the panels.",
      "**Don't** let colour alone carry a state, or use a state colour as decoration.",
      "**Don't** set labels in uppercase with wide tracking. Labels are sentence case at 0.75rem/500.",
      "**Don't** use the site's purple secondary in the panels.",
      "**Don't** apply this file's rules to the site home, which keeps its own look."
    ]
  }
